{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00137",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.89,
      "end_seconds": 3.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. Where would you like me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.37,
      "end_seconds": 8.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Yes, do sit. Tell me what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 8.71,
      "end_seconds": 15.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.67,
      "text": "It's a high fever, mostly. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.83,
      "end_seconds": 19.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "And when did that start? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.16,
      "end_seconds": 26.47,
      "duration_seconds": 6.31,
      "text": "Okay, so it's been three days now. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.1,
      "end_seconds": 34.75,
      "duration_seconds": 7.65,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.2,
      "end_seconds": 47.3,
      "duration_seconds": 11.1,
      "text": "It settles a little with paracetamol. Pretty severe, if I'm being honest. My family kept telling me to get it checked. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.73,
      "end_seconds": 52.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Sorry, I'm just writing a few notes, bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.45,
      "end_seconds": 55.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "No problem, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.35,
      "end_seconds": 59.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Have you had any bleeding from the gums?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.89,
      "end_seconds": 63.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "No, no bleeding from the gums."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.64,
      "end_seconds": 66.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Mm-hm. Have you had any cough or breathlessness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.52,
      "end_seconds": 69.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.59,
      "end_seconds": 70.29,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.97,
      "end_seconds": 73.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "I'll just check what's already recorded here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.43,
      "end_seconds": 75.33,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "Please do."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.83,
      "end_seconds": 89.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.33,
      "end_seconds": 97.37,
      "duration_seconds": 6.04,
      "text": "I mean, I take aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day for my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.95,
      "end_seconds": 101.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Sorry, the computer needs a moment to load this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.81,
      "end_seconds": 102.57,
      "duration_seconds": 0.76,
      "text": "No rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.94,
      "end_seconds": 118.25,
      "duration_seconds": 6.31,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Right, do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.48,
      "end_seconds": 122.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Not that I know, um, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.12,
      "end_seconds": 140.67,
      "duration_seconds": 17.55,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.17,
      "end_seconds": 145.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.74,
      "end_seconds": 150.73,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.05,
      "end_seconds": 154.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Yes, I had a bypass operation, six years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.45,
      "end_seconds": 161.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Is there anything you were hoping to get out of today's visit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.56,
      "end_seconds": 164.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Mostly I just want to understand what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.82,
      "end_seconds": 169.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.09,
      "end_seconds": 175.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Yes, heart disease. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.73,
      "end_seconds": 188.09,
      "duration_seconds": 11.36,
      "text": "I like to make sure you understand what's happening, so please stop me at any point. There are no silly questions, and I'd much rather you ask now than go home still wondering about something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.54,
      "end_seconds": 191.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Right, I understand now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.31,
      "end_seconds": 194.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "How's everything else at home otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.63,
      "end_seconds": 200.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "Well, busy. Everyone's running in different directions at the moment, you know how it is."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.83,
      "end_seconds": 207.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Do you have any questions before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.82,
      "end_seconds": 219.56,
      "duration_seconds": 10.74,
      "text": "Uh, not at the moment, I think you've covered most of what I was wondering. If something comes to mind later, I'll ask you before I leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.11,
      "end_seconds": 230.17,
      "duration_seconds": 9.06,
      "text": "So, based on your history, my working impression is a viral fever, possibly dengue. The reason I say that is that the way you describe it fits together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.68,
      "end_seconds": 232.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Well, doctor, is this dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.19,
      "end_seconds": 247.55,
      "duration_seconds": 14.36,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a viral fever, possibly dengue do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a high fever for three days, severe, and no breathlessness or cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.46,
      "end_seconds": 251.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Yes, you know, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.99,
      "end_seconds": 254.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.96,
      "end_seconds": 262.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Yes, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.13,
      "end_seconds": 280.97,
      "duration_seconds": 17.84,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a dengue test for fever. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. Let's use paracetamol, 500 milligrams, every six hours if needed, for three days. That's for fever and body aches. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 281.42,
      "end_seconds": 284.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Alright, I'll pick it up today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.41,
      "end_seconds": 310.25,
      "duration_seconds": 24.84,
      "text": "Drink a lot, coconut water, ORS, whatever you can manage. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. If you notice any bleeding or you can't keep fluids down, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department. Please come and see me after the results are back. Tell me what you've taken from all that, so I can fill in any gaps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 311.58,
      "end_seconds": 321.08,
      "duration_seconds": 9.5,
      "text": "So, I take the paracetamol, 500 milligrams, every six hours if needed and come back after the results are back. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.45,
      "end_seconds": 325.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Alright, that's everything from me. Any other questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.49,
      "end_seconds": 330.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "I think that's clear. Thank you for being so thorough."
    }
  ]
}